1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,000
Το Plex ζήτησε 120€ για να συνεχίσετε να βλέπετε από τις συσκευές σας.
Το πλήρωσα εγώ το ποσό.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Αν χρησιμοποιείτε συχνά και μπορείτε,
 οποιαδήποτε συμβολή θα εκτιμηθεί.

3
00:00:07,030 --> 00:00:09,790
This place seems to have a lot of shops.

4
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,890
It'll be worth shopping around.

5
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:18,710
This is a lively town.

6
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:20,380
I see a lot of bars.

7
00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:24,510
Oh, right. Frieren, let's go
shopping together later.

8
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:27,990
This place seems to have
a lot of nice shops.

9
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:30,280
If you want.

10
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:37,530
What are you doing, Frieren? Let's go.

11
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:47,080
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

12
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:49,500
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

13
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:52,420
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

14
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:54,050
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

15
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:56,380
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

16
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:58,720
<i>Across this land</i>

17
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:01,050
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

18
00:01:01,050 --> 00:01:03,510
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

19
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:15,820
<i>The story ends</i>

20
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:18,320
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

21
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:21,160
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

22
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,830
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

23
00:01:22,830 --> 00:01:25,330
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

24
00:01:25,330 --> 00:01:27,500
<i>Makes people forget</i>

25
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:30,290
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

26
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:32,080
<i>Begin to rust</i>

27
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:33,920
<i>Just the same</i>

28
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:36,210
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

29
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:39,550
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

30
00:01:39,550 --> 00:01:41,430
<i>And they live on</i>

31
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:43,970
<i>We chose the same path</i>

32
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:46,100
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

33
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:47,640
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

34
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:51,900
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

35
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,270
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

36
00:01:53,270 --> 00:01:54,360
<i>Even now</i>

37
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:56,730
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

38
00:01:56,730 --> 00:02:00,280
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

39
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,950
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

40
00:02:17,650 --> 00:02:20,120
You don't need to be so harsh!

41
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:22,230
You're always so rude to me!

42
00:02:22,230 --> 00:02:24,790
Do you really hate me that much?

43
00:02:24,790 --> 00:02:27,100
Forget it! I'm going back to my master!

44
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:35,500
Would it kill her to listen
to me once in a while?

45
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:38,230
What's all the noise about?

46
00:02:38,230 --> 00:02:39,610
Are the lovebirds fighting?

47
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:47,230
It's Fern's birthday today,
but Stark didn't get her a present.

48
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:49,620
Fern is furious.

49
00:02:48,370 --> 00:02:49,980
Hmph.

50
00:02:51,970 --> 00:02:54,840
Honestly, I think you were too harsh today.

51
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:58,370
You never listen to anything Stark says.

52
00:03:00,930 --> 00:03:03,430
I didn't get her anything either.

53
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:09,630
Men don't care about little things
like birthdays and anniversaries.

54
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:11,380
Ow!

55
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:14,820
Okay, okay. I'll buy you something,
so stop kicking me.

56
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:16,930
My knees are gonna be sore later.

57
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:25,460
I feel sorry for Stark.

58
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:29,180
I'm old enough to let most callousness go,

59
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:33,800
but girls can make the emotions
of boys his age swing wildly.

60
00:03:39,810 --> 00:03:41,750
I think you should go after him.

61
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:49,070
Maybe you should go see him.

62
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:24,630
That's right. Her hair ornament has
a butterfly on it, too.

63
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:28,440
That's a cute pouch.

64
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,470
You don't like it?

65
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:33,060
I don't like how accustomed you seem
to the company of women.

66
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:34,730
I see.

67
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:37,720
Did you find Stark?

68
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:40,430
He was in the plaza.

69
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:43,290
But you couldn't talk to him, huh?

70
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:48,890
I get it. It's not that you don't like him.

71
00:04:48,890 --> 00:04:52,290
You just don't know how to
interact with boys your age.

72
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,230
Ah, to be young.

73
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:57,490
No matter. Choose whatever you want.

74
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:59,750
We can check out other stores, too.

75
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:05,010
No, it's fine.

76
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:09,140
Then I'll choose something for you.

77
00:05:10,390 --> 00:05:14,310
Anyway, even if he forgot to get you
a gift, I think you overreacted.

78
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:17,660
He's not that conscientious.

79
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:20,930
I doubt he even remembers his own birthday.

80
00:05:20,930 --> 00:05:22,490
You shouldn't blame him.

81
00:05:23,350 --> 00:05:26,730
I gave Mr. Stark a present on his birthday.

82
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:30,000
Really? Did you choose one with him?

83
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:31,750
How did you know?

84
00:05:32,520 --> 00:05:37,180
Normally, no one declines when someone
offers to buy them whatever they want.

85
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:41,050
You must consider it an important memory.

86
00:05:41,050 --> 00:05:42,500
That's why you said no.

87
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:45,010
I don't know.

88
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:48,500
I just felt like it.

89
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,250
I see.

90
00:05:51,290 --> 00:05:55,380
Then go apologize to Stark
and pick out a gift with him.

91
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:02,090
He's just a kid. He's slow on the uptake.

92
00:06:03,590 --> 00:06:05,410
You want to make up with him, don't you?

93
00:06:06,690 --> 00:06:09,660
People won't know how you feel
unless you tell them.

94
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:14,310
You're right.

95
00:06:15,010 --> 00:06:16,860
I'm heading back to the inn.

96
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:17,530
Um...

97
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:20,410
I'm sorry for kicking you.

98
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:38,700
Mr. Stark.

99
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:44,230
Fern.

100
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:51,000
I—

101
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:51,310
Sorry!

102
00:06:55,150 --> 00:07:01,830
I wanted to choose a gift with you,
since I don't know what you like.

103
00:07:02,890 --> 00:07:09,550
But I thought you'd get upset with me
again if I said that, so I couldn't.

104
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:12,960
I wouldn't be upset with you.

105
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:19,200
Mr. Stark, I'm sorry. I was too harsh.

106
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:24,020
It's fine. I'm used to it.

107
00:07:24,530 --> 00:07:26,490
I'm really sorry.

108
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:30,360
Let's go.

109
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:33,510
Okay.

110
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:49,890
You're spying on them?

111
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:52,130
That's in poor taste, Frieren.

112
00:07:52,530 --> 00:07:54,130
Same to you, Sein.

113
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,710
Looks like they made up.

114
00:08:00,530 --> 00:08:04,730
You understand relationships better
once you're older.

115
00:08:04,730 --> 00:08:07,150
You start avoiding conflict then.

116
00:08:09,290 --> 00:08:11,780
Those arguments are the
privilege of the young.

117
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:14,970
That can't have been easy for you, Frieren.

118
00:08:14,970 --> 00:08:16,910
Looking after two kids sounds tough.

119
00:08:19,670 --> 00:08:21,600
What do you mean by
understanding relationships?

120
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:23,400
So it's three kids.

121
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:30,840
Fern asked me for advice instead of you.

122
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:35,720
I wonder who she's comparing me to.

123
00:08:36,410 --> 00:08:39,380
Fern was raised by Heiter.

124
00:08:39,990 --> 00:08:44,100
She shouldn't be comparing me
to such a great priest.

125
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,050
I'd hardly call him great.

126
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:49,530
He was a drunk and often hungover.

127
00:08:49,530 --> 00:08:50,810
Has he become an undead?

128
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:53,510
He was picky with his food, too.

129
00:08:53,510 --> 00:08:54,400
Quit it.

130
00:08:54,670 --> 00:08:56,360
And he lied all the time.

131
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,150
I haven't had anything to drink.

132
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:01,270
He was just a corrupt priest.

133
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:04,830
You're even more depraved, though.

134
00:09:04,830 --> 00:09:06,040
Sorry about that.

135
00:09:07,410 --> 00:09:09,610
I'm surprised, though.

136
00:09:09,610 --> 00:09:14,500
The Mr. Heiter I remember was
a kind and dependable old man.

137
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:18,500
Unlike me, he was an ideal grown-up.

138
00:09:21,490 --> 00:09:23,750
Heiter, you've changed.

139
00:09:23,750 --> 00:09:25,360
You've matured.

140
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:30,260
What are you talking about? I'm an old man.

141
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:33,430
It happens naturally as people age.

142
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:35,440
Huh.

143
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:38,320
I wish I could say that, anyway,

144
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:43,580
but the truth is, my mind has
hardly changed since I was a child.

145
00:09:44,010 --> 00:09:51,030
I've simply been pretending to be an adult
until I can make it as an ideal grown-up.

146
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:56,080
I'll probably keep pretending
until the day I die.

147
00:09:56,580 --> 00:10:01,960
Children need grown-ups
for emotional support.

148
00:10:02,850 --> 00:10:04,970
Fern in particular is the hardworking sort.

149
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:08,730
She needs lots of praise and guidance.

150
00:10:09,390 --> 00:10:14,970
Then who will praise you for
pretending until the day you die?

151
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:19,320
That's what the Goddess is for,

152
00:10:20,060 --> 00:10:23,120
though I'll have to wait until I go
to heaven to receive my reward.

153
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:26,360
Then I'll praise you down here.

154
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:29,480
You will?

155
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:34,680
But I'm a human. I doubt you
understand how I feel.

156
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:37,020
How do you intend to praise me?

157
00:10:48,810 --> 00:10:51,810
That was better than I expected.

158
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:58,970
Frieren, once I go to heaven,
I'll speak with the Goddess for you.

159
00:10:58,970 --> 00:11:03,380
You should be praised by her.

160
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:06,380
Oh? Then I'll look forward to it.

161
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:14,470
What do you think you're doing, Frieren?

162
00:11:14,830 --> 00:11:17,720
I think you're a proper adult, Sein.

163
00:11:23,530 --> 00:11:26,980
I would've loved to have
an older woman do this.

164
00:11:27,590 --> 00:11:28,980
You should be glad, then.

165
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:32,550
Few women are older than me.

166
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:42,650
Thank you.

167
00:11:42,650 --> 00:11:46,410
There weren't any passenger carriages
around here, so we appreciate it.

168
00:11:46,410 --> 00:11:49,000
We help each other when we're in need.

169
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,710
I'm actually a merchant in the town up ahead.

170
00:11:52,710 --> 00:11:55,380
I run an accessory shop there.

171
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:57,660
Are you interested?

172
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:59,380
You're a good salesman.

173
00:11:59,790 --> 00:12:05,000
I'm not too interested, but Fern
likes that kind of thing. Don't you?

174
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:05,620
Huh?

175
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:08,510
Did you buy a new bracelet?

176
00:12:09,670 --> 00:12:12,550
Um, this is...

177
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,420
That's a cute design.

178
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:18,010
I have a ring with the same design.

179
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:21,360
Himmel gave it to me.

180
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:23,150
It probably matches yours.

181
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:24,930
Really?

182
00:12:24,930 --> 00:12:27,970
Now where did I put it?

183
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,060
Huh?

184
00:12:33,550 --> 00:12:36,710
You're so disorganized.

185
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:38,850
Found it.

186
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:53,840
Sorry. I let my guard down.

187
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:59,100
Avian monsters are cunning
and skilled at concealing their mana.

188
00:13:00,170 --> 00:13:01,620
What are we going to do?

189
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:08,980
Can't we figure something out with flying
magic after defeating the monster?

190
00:13:09,550 --> 00:13:11,980
You can make a carriage levitate, right?

191
00:13:12,210 --> 00:13:15,960
Stark, have you ever seen a flying carriage?

192
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,010
We're in one right now.

193
00:13:17,790 --> 00:13:24,770
This may surprise you, but it's only been
forty years since humankind learned to fly.

194
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:29,200
Until then, the skies were the
exclusive domain of demons and monsters.

195
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:35,230
The flying magic we use is
a repurposed demon spell.

196
00:13:35,230 --> 00:13:39,230
Spare me the details and
dumb it down for me.

197
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:42,930
It means we can't adapt it
because we copied their technique

198
00:13:42,930 --> 00:13:44,870
without understanding
the principles behind it.

199
00:13:45,170 --> 00:13:49,210
Things larger than humans
can only be made to fly briefly.

200
00:13:49,210 --> 00:13:50,800
I see.

201
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,370
We'll have to get out.

202
00:13:53,030 --> 00:13:55,470
I'll fly out with the merchant.

203
00:13:55,470 --> 00:13:57,260
Fern, could you take Sein?

204
00:13:57,260 --> 00:13:58,380
Understood.

205
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:00,300
I'll get my cargo together.

206
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,250
What about me?

207
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:05,020
You can jump down.

208
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:06,500
What are you talking about?

209
00:14:06,890 --> 00:14:08,990
I'm pretty sure that would kill me.

210
00:14:08,990 --> 00:14:11,520
You're a warrior. A fall from
this height won't kill you.

211
00:14:11,930 --> 00:14:13,480
Of course it would kill me!

212
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:15,840
Don't act like you don't understand that!

213
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,010
That's odd.

214
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:21,890
Eisen was never injured by
a free fall from any height.

215
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:31,180
What is wrong with him?

216
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,020
Heiter was appalled.

217
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:37,450
That just goes to show that Mr. Eisen
was far from normal.

218
00:14:38,350 --> 00:14:43,420
What about levitating the carriage
just before it hits the ground?

219
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:46,790
I'll need to calculate
if I can stop a free fall.

220
00:14:47,140 --> 00:14:51,640
If I don't reduce the force sufficiently,
we'll be ground into minced meat.

221
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,560
That sounds horrifying!

222
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:57,550
Either way, we should probably hurry.

223
00:14:57,870 --> 00:15:02,310
This type of monster hunts by
slamming its prey into the ground.

224
00:15:03,070 --> 00:15:04,040
I see.

225
00:15:16,190 --> 00:15:18,770
Well, it's worth a shot.

226
00:15:20,880 --> 00:15:24,130
Don't just drop us!

227
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:37,670
W-We're alive.

228
00:15:37,670 --> 00:15:39,970
It seems like the plan was a success.

229
00:15:40,350 --> 00:15:41,720
You call that a success?

230
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:43,830
You call that a plan?

231
00:15:46,530 --> 00:15:49,480
The horse is only slightly injured.
I've finished treating it.

232
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:53,110
But the carriage is a wreck.
It needs repairs.

233
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:54,870
Sorry.

234
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:56,970
No, thank you.

235
00:15:56,970 --> 00:15:59,490
If it'd just been me, I'd be dead.

236
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:02,260
It'll take a while to fix the carriage.

237
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:17,690
Huh?

238
00:16:18,370 --> 00:16:19,520
That's odd.

239
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:22,350
Where did it go?

240
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:28,390
It's gotten warmer lately.

241
00:16:28,390 --> 00:16:30,360
Should we start dressing lighter?

242
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:34,020
By the way, Fern, that bracelet...

243
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:38,030
It was a birthday present from Mr. Stark.

244
00:16:38,510 --> 00:16:41,060
I spent three hours choosing a gift.

245
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:43,460
You ended up choosing it?

246
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:46,090
I asked him to choose what he wanted.

247
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:49,170
Oh, I see.

248
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:51,770
That must've been difficult, Stark.

249
00:16:51,770 --> 00:16:54,080
Her type is the hardest to deal with.

250
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,150
Yeah.

251
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:58,970
<i>Will she like this?</i>

252
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:02,390
I spent three hours gauging her reactions.

253
00:17:02,690 --> 00:17:04,910
I felt like I was dying.

254
00:17:04,910 --> 00:17:06,350
Poor kid.

255
00:17:07,090 --> 00:17:08,860
<i>I can hear everything they're saying.</i>

256
00:17:09,390 --> 00:17:10,350
But...

257
00:17:11,450 --> 00:17:13,830
I'm glad I did, since she likes it.

258
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,890
Anyway, good going, Stark.

259
00:17:21,890 --> 00:17:24,430
I didn't think you knew what you were doing.

260
00:17:25,130 --> 00:17:27,210
That design is of a mirrored lotus.

261
00:17:27,210 --> 00:17:29,670
In the language of flowers,
it means "eternal love."

262
00:17:29,950 --> 00:17:33,170
In this area, people give them
to their lovers.

263
00:17:34,990 --> 00:17:36,070
Mr. Stark?

264
00:17:36,070 --> 00:17:37,930
I-I didn't know!

265
00:17:38,180 --> 00:17:39,510
This is all a misunderstanding.

266
00:17:39,510 --> 00:17:41,880
You think I know the language of flowers?

267
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:44,320
That's fair enough. You're an idiot, after all.

268
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:46,150
You're being even harsher than usual!

269
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,640
It's not like you knew either.

270
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:51,320
Did you say something?

271
00:17:51,750 --> 00:17:53,110
It's nothing.

272
00:17:54,150 --> 00:17:56,900
Should I buy you a replacement?

273
00:17:57,970 --> 00:18:01,990
You put a lot of effort into
choosing this gift for me.

274
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,760
Don't ever say that again.

275
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:07,480
Sorry.

276
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:13,920
What is it?

277
00:18:15,550 --> 00:18:17,320
Nothing.

278
00:19:21,970 --> 00:19:23,160
Ms. Frieren.

279
00:19:24,310 --> 00:19:26,370
We've finished repairing the carriage.

280
00:19:26,370 --> 00:19:28,740
We'll depart early tomorrow morning.

281
00:19:29,130 --> 00:19:30,020
I see.

282
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:33,220
You've been slipping out every night.

283
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:35,120
What are you looking for?

284
00:19:35,540 --> 00:19:37,640
The ring Himmel gave me.

285
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:40,020
I'll help.

286
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:43,070
We'll wait to depart until we've found it.

287
00:19:43,550 --> 00:19:44,500
No.

288
00:19:45,150 --> 00:19:48,100
If I don't find it tonight,
I'll give up on it.

289
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:50,190
I'm used to losing things.

290
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:54,020
Besides, that's not the
only thing Himmel gave me.

291
00:19:54,490 --> 00:19:58,470
Wasn't it a mirrored-lotus
design ring like this one?

292
00:19:58,690 --> 00:20:01,410
In the language of flowers,
it means "eternal love."

293
00:20:01,410 --> 00:20:03,670
Does it? I didn't know.

294
00:20:04,630 --> 00:20:09,240
It doesn't matter. I doubt Himmel
knew what it meant either.

295
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:12,870
Regardless, I'm sure it's important.

296
00:20:13,530 --> 00:20:15,440
Let's look for it together.

297
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:20,680
You should've told me.

298
00:20:21,050 --> 00:20:26,170
A few people in my village have
lost accessories over the years.

299
00:20:26,750 --> 00:20:30,250
I intended to give you this spell
for finding lost accessories

300
00:20:30,250 --> 00:20:34,320
as a reward for your assistance.

301
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:56,720
<i>Frieren.</i>

302
00:20:57,920 --> 00:21:01,400
You worked really hard
to defeat the Demon King.

303
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,430
Choose whatever you'd like.

304
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:05,200
An accessory, huh?

305
00:21:06,170 --> 00:21:08,810
I would've preferred
something from a magic shop.

306
00:21:09,070 --> 00:21:10,660
This one will do.

307
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:13,690
That was quick. Put more thought into it.

308
00:21:16,690 --> 00:21:17,760
What's wrong?

309
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:20,410
Nothing.

310
00:21:41,510 --> 00:21:42,420
Frieren.

311
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:44,370
Thank you.

312
00:22:22,350 --> 00:22:25,830
Aren't you glad you didn't
give up, Ms. Frieren?

313
00:22:33,530 --> 00:22:34,940
Maybe.

314
00:22:38,750 --> 00:22:42,920
By the way, why are you wearing
a mirrored-lotus bracelet?

315
00:22:42,920 --> 00:22:45,050
Because Mr. Stark is an idiot.

316
00:22:46,410 --> 00:22:47,550
How could you say that?

317
00:22:49,990 --> 00:22:52,530
<i>And you alright</i>

318
00:22:53,030 --> 00:22:55,040
<i>Can you hear me</i>

319
00:22:55,830 --> 00:23:01,920
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

320
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:04,250
<i>Crying excessively</i>

321
00:23:04,840 --> 00:23:07,420
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

322
00:23:07,420 --> 00:23:13,470
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

323
00:23:13,470 --> 00:23:17,180
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

324
00:23:17,180 --> 00:23:19,940
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

325
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:25,610
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

326
00:23:25,610 --> 00:23:29,150
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

327
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:32,200
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

328
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:36,950
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

329
00:23:36,950 --> 00:23:43,040
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

330
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:48,880
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

331
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:54,890
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

332
00:23:54,890 --> 00:24:00,640
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

333
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:03,600
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

334
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:06,520
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

335
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:12,700
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

336
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:15,370
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

337
00:24:15,370 --> 00:24:19,290
<i>for you to come back home</i>

338
00:24:20,020 --> 00:24:22,830
I have battle magic, too.

339
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:21,960
I feel anxious.

340
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:24,020
He doesn't have his brother's talent.

341
00:24:22,230 --> 00:24:23,720
Yes, Father.

342
00:24:22,820 --> 00:24:24,830
This is starting to look bad.

343
00:24:23,830 --> 00:24:26,310
In any case, it looks like we should hurry.

344
00:24:24,830 --> 00:24:26,310
It's hell.

345
00:24:26,310 --> 00:24:28,420
This smells like trouble.

346
00:24:28,420 --> 00:24:30,420
Let's head to the next village.
